{
  "schema_version": 2,
  "source": "# Observatory field notes\n\nMirror cleaning removes surface dust without scratching the coating. The technician first lifts loose grit with a soft air bulb. A clean cloth stays inside its sealed pouch.\n\nThe rinse bottle has a blue cap. A final distilled-water rinse prevents mineral marks on the telescope mirror. The optic dries upright for twenty minutes.\n\nThe lamp stands beside the workbench. The operator tilts the glass under the lamp to reveal residue. Inspection after washing confirms that the mirror surface is clean.\n\nPublic observing sessions require a timed visitor reservation. The evening gate opens at 20:30. A reservation covers one adult and one child.\n\nThe printed booking slip includes a star symbol. Visitor reservations remain valid in cloudy weather because the indoor planetarium stays open. Clouds do not trigger an automatic refund.\n\nThe last bus leaves at 23:10. Visitors must leave the telescope terrace ten minutes before the bus. The departure schedule gives guests time to reach transport safely.\n",
  "source_name": "observatory.md",
